    "durationMs": 283146,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified — 33/33 checks pass, including a restart test.\n\n**What I built** (Laravel 11.57.1, moved in via Composer since `/workspace` only had `.git`):\n\n- **Migration + `Link` model** — `links` table with a case-sensitive unique `code` (utf8mb4_bin), `text` url, `unsignedBigInteger clicks` defaulting to 0; Eloquent with an integer cast.\n- **`LinkController`** — `POST /links` (201 with `{code, url, clicks: 0}`, generated 8-char codes when `code` is omitted, 409 on duplicate custom codes backed by the unique index), `GET /links` (`{items, total}`, ascending by id), `GET /links/{code}`, and `GET /r/{code}` (302 with an exact `Location` header, atomic `clicks = clicks + 1` increment). All errors (409/404/422, including malformed JSON) are always JSON with an `error` field, validated with a closure rule enforcing absolute http/https URLs with a host and codes of 4–20 `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`.\n- **Routing** — registered in `routes/api.php` with `apiPrefix: ''` in `bootstrap/app.php`, so paths are exactly `/links` and `/r/{code}`; the api group carries no throttle (verified in framework source), so no 429 risk.\n- **DB config** — `.env` contains no DB credentials; everything comes from the `DB_*` environment variables. I confirmed in `ServeCommand` source why `--no-reload` matters: without it, `DB_*` vars are explicitly stripped from the server process.\n- **`start.sh`** (executable) — ensures the database exists, runs `php artisan migrate --force`, then `exec php artisan serve --host=0.0.0.0 --port=8000 --no-reload` in the foreground.\n- **README** — endpoints plus a \"Starting the server\" section.\n\n**Verification highlights**: created/retrieved links with URLs returned byte-for-byte unchanged (query strings, fragments, uppercase schemes), 10 concurrent clicks counted exactly once, all 11 invalid-input cases returned 422, and after killing and restarting via `sh start.sh` the links and click counts (e.g. 11 clicks) survived. Test data was cleared afterward, and no servers were left running."
  }
